 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 519169,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "If a student takes out a private student loan for $9,800 at 5.99% interest but does not begin paying it back for 66 months, how much is then owed on the loan?",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>The amount due for a loan, <i>A</i>, when the principal, <i>P</i>, an interest rate of <i>r</i> (in decimal form), compounded <i>n</i> times per year for <i>t</i> years is found using the formula <span data-math=\"A = P{\\left( {1 + \\frac{r}{n}} \\right)^{nt}}\"></span>.</p>\n<p>You are told the number of compounding periods.</p>\n<p><i><span data-math=\"nt = 66\"></span></i></p>\n<p>Use those parentheses in your calculator, too!</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"A = 9,800{\\left( {1 + \\frac{{0.0599}}{{12}}} \\right)^{66}}\"></span></p>\n<p><span data-math=\"A = {\\text{ }}\\$13,612.83\"></span></p>\n"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "$13,028.61"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  }
 ],
